Local container definitions:
* To build a single image:
  podman build --squash --tag localhost/my-image:<version# OR latest> DirPathToContainerfile/
  https://containertoolbx.org/doc/#custom-images
* To build/update and (re)deploy all defined run update_all.sh
  * Note: this will delete the existing containers and images, make sure changes are backed up

How to create a definition:
# Create a directory to track the new toolbox image
# If files should be deployed image, create a 'root' folder in the container for them
# Containerfile is built as expected, see existing examples or https://containertoolbx.org/doc/#custom-images
#* The root folder is not part of the standard, it could be anything. Just make sure it is implemented in Containerfile
# Optional - Any container setup/teardown scripting should be in:
#* root/usr/local/bin/oncreate.sh
#* root/usr/local/bin/ondelete.sh


The Containerfile can then be built to create a my-fedora-toolbox:42 image:

[user@hostname ~]$ podman build \
                     --squash \
                     --tag localhost/my-fedora-toolbox:42 \
                     /path/to/Containerfile/dir

